      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "OUR KIWI PRINCESS (5) gets top billing after two sound thirds, the latest a long-neck defeat at Leonora when she was still there at the finish at generous odds. Her established record around 1400m and strong association with Kyra Yuill give her a reliable profile. REPEATER (3) has the sharpest rebound case: the Leonora mile run was poor, but his Mingenew win two back was decisive and he is better judged returning to a distance range where he has already won. CLIMB ON TOP (1) brings the winning form, having scored at Moora and Broome at his past two, though the 1400m and big weight keep him more of a strong danger than a clear standout. SHASFA (6) has been close enough in recent fourths to hold place claims, with her previous 1400m wins keeping her in the mix if she finds a shade more at the end of the race. The old boy LACEVINSKY (2) isn't out of this on his best form.",
